Upstream: citeproc-js (src/citeproc/, 2026-10-08, GitHub #790, #791)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

`src/citeproc/` is a port, in stages (#792 to #797), of citeproc-js, Zotero's
CSL engine. #791 laid down the skeleton and the verification harness only;
no engine code is translated yet.

  citeproc-js   https://github.com/juris-m/citeproc-js
                version 2.4.63, commit 73bc1b44bc7d54d0bfec4e070fd27f5efe024ff9
                Copyright (c) 2009-2019 Frank Bennett

The grant. `LICENSE` at that commit, and the header of the published bundle,
say: the Common Public Attribution License Version 1.0 (CPAL-1.0) or later,
OR the GNU Affero General Public License version 3 or later. The repository
ships the full AGPLv3 text as its `AGPLv3` file. We take the AGPL option: the
port is AGPL-3.0 (this crate is AGPL-3.0-only), and every ported file's header
names the upstream file(s), version and commit, the copyright line, the
licence, a modified-work notice with its date (AGPL-3.0 section 5a) and the
no-warranty statement (sections 4 and 5).

A metadata mismatch, recorded. The npm `package.json` of citeproc 2.4.63 says
`"license": "CPAL-1.0 OR AGPL-1.0"`. That contradicts the licence text in the
same package; the text governs. AGPL-1.0, the old Affero GPL, would not be
compatible with this crate, and is not what we take.

Where the port lives. Only in AGPL crates (section 5c): `src/citeproc/` of
this crate. It never goes into a GPL-only crate or into anything published
under another licence. The repository is public (sections 6, 13); any
network-served use keeps the source link the kovan-web UI shows.

